Z||000038||DISenchanted||02-01-2000||05:51 AM||||On the IMSA kit, is it just a new rear with wider fenders so you can add bigger tires?  I'm trying to figure out what exactly is involved.||||reg||1
Z||000039||william_thorniii||02-01-2000||08:58 AM||||DIS,<P>The front and rear fenders have serious bulges for the tires.  Other than that there is a front and rear spoiler.  It is a fairly simple kit as far as they go, but for $3500 from IRM, I think that it is unreasonable for 5 slightly modified panels.  It seems to me that the easiest way to create this kit would be to find donor fenders to keep the same lines and then glas to them.  The price of used parts would have to be lower than the price of that much glass.  Also the molds would be much smaller and therefore keep the cost down.  <P>For a good look at an IMSA notchback check out Jamie Jones at <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/customer.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/customer.htm</A> <P>This should show you all necessary angles.  Again if you should have any questions about this feel free to contact me off of the list.<P>Many Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
